 "text": "Hey there, how are you? Get up every thirty minutes or so and stretch for minute. It makes a big difference. Then stand up tall and reach your hands down as far as you can, then stretch the sides of your body. Hold for a few seconds. Try it at first, but with a small pillow under your laptop and another under your hands. That's usually the chair pushing you forward. Try leaning slightly backward and lift your arms and neck off the desk. It straightens your neck and shoulders.",
